cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use exosat-rv in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "exosat-rv: an independent reproduction of the first exosatellite radial-velocity detection"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline that reproduces, from public ESO archive data, the first radial-velocity
  detection of a satellite around a substellar object — a planetary-mass companion to the
  brown dwarf CD-35 2722 B (Hoy et al. 2026). It inventories the CRIRES+ holdings, converts
  ESO ADP spectra losslessly into the cr2res layout that the viper RV code consumes, extracts
  velocities, and tests the published model comparison against an independent fitter. The
  paper's conclusion reproduces from its published radial velocities; the velocities
  themselves do not yet reproduce from the archive, and a positive control on the known
  binary brown dwarf GJ 229 B establishes that the shortfall is precision rather than a
  broken extraction. Every claim the project published and later found false is indexed in
  HANDOFF.md. No discovery is claimed and nothing is submitted anywhere.
